0..72 Comment "// The quasi-inverse and the equivalence between two types, and the maps"
73..137 Comment "// between them, after the HoTT book\'s § 4.3 and cubical Agda\'s"
138..211 Comment "// `Cubical/Foundations/Isomorphism.agda` (`isoToEquiv`). `A ≅ B`, also"
212..288 Comment "// written `Iso(A, B)`, is the record of a map, a map back and the two round"
289..365 Comment "// trips. `A ≃ B`, also written `A <~> B`, is the bi-invertible map: a map"
366..437 Comment "// with a left inverse and a right inverse, each a record of its own. A"
438..509 Comment "// quasi-inverse is bi-invertible at once, its map back serving as both"
510..588 Comment "// inverses. A bi-invertible map is a quasi-inverse by its left inverse, whose"
589..663 Comment "// second round trip passes through the right one: the two inverses agree,"
664..694 Comment "// `h(y) = g(t(h(y))) = g(y)`."
696..771 Comment "/// A quasi-inverse is bi-invertible: its map back is both the left and the"
772..815 Comment "/// right inverse (cubical\'s `isoToEquiv`)."
